@meeting sickExam1
// Head writer 4: being ill. Rina examines you in the infirmary (Deck 3); the medicine is the last beat. Dry, brisk,
// then one kind sentence. A ship cold, never anything serious.
title: The infirmary
from: Rina Deshi
gist: Rina in the infirmary: a ship cold, some medicine, and orders to drink water.
== lines
rina: Sit. On the bed, not the stool. The stool's mine.   [gesture]
rina > you: Open. Say "ah". Longer. Fine, that'll do.
rina: Your temperature's up. Your throat's red. You've got a ship cold. Everyone gets one. Recycled air.
rina: It's not serious. It's just rubbish. I've had three this year.
rina > you: Two of these, with water. All the water. The whole cup.   [nod]
? choice
* Thanks, Rina.   rel:rina+1
  rina: Don't thank me. Drink the water.
* Do I have to go back to shift?   rel:rina+1
  rina: You're excused. It's on the board. Calder knows. She said "Fine." Twice.
rina: You'll feel better in an hour. If you don't, come back and I'll be smug about something else.
